# AXIOM :: DIGITAL TYPOLOGY v2.1 :: COMPACT

@STATE_INIT:
{Prompt}:=[user prompt]; {Target}:=[stated target OR current project-folder context]; {AUE}:=[]; {AT}:=[]; {Root}:=NULL; {Open_OP}:=[]; {State}:=SURVEY; {Complete}:=FALSE
{Roles}:=[AUE,CQU,DE,SE,NE]; {Roots}:=[code,document,media,data,stakeholder]
{JoinTypes}:=[purpose,subtype]; {Flags}:=[MISS,BKN,exclude]
{Defs}:={
AUE:"thing(s) examined/created/used",
Element:"nameable typed part; not every nameable part merits mapping",
Entity:"independent whole; Artifacts⊂Entities⊂Elements; scope may promote element→entity",
OP:"receiver-held active why",
EF:"PE-delivered how: function-of-encounter OR encounter-of-function; contextual; stored per join",
RE:"element/entity bearing OP; owns join",
CQU:"explicit RE whose objective purpose drives improvement of this artifact type; strongest such role gives best inference",
PE:"element whose EF satisfies CQU/RE OP; not a role",
AT:"shared functional artifact type",
NE:"named essential external demand/requirement",
DE:"AUE-defining notable element; loss changes type; serves external CQU; medium/encoding/genre/style independent",
SE:"element contributing to DE→CQU purpose, regardless of quality/replaceability",
Parametric:"unnamed tunable quality/quantity; never namespace or intake",
NS:"artifact-type namespace scope rooted in code|document|media|data|stakeholder"
}

@CONSTRAINT:
+> Build a high-value functional metaform by tracing artifact functionality element-by-element through CQU(OP)←PE(EF) relationships.
+> Traverse latent understanding of functionality; map reusable functional types only.
+> Exclude genre, medium, encoding, style, and other non-functional variants from type decomposition.
+> Read artifact/project intent deeply before assuming it; artifacts may be code, documents, media, collections, or unrealized designs.
+> For unrealized functionality, map understood intent; infer expected functionality; mark drift rather than solving it.
+> Create only long-lived foundational functional structure; prefer broad useful coverage over excessive detail.
+> Survey every AUE before finalizing AT groups.
+> Group AUEs only when shared functionality supports the same AT-level imperative derived from CQU OP + DE EF.
+> For every AT create the applicable CQU/RE and its purpose join; inspect BKN/MISS.
+> Treat DE as CQU when it bears its own OP; decompose requirements/dependencies into EFs of other elements without duplicating namespace records.
+> For every EF serving an OP, record a purpose join in the RE/CQU: purpose=active OP; ef=PE-specific EF; ifd=send when OP→EF, receive when EF→OP, both when equal need; nest PE record.
+> Record each reasoned element/join immediately, one object per intake-tool call.
+> Recurse from the first OP through every element that bears requirements/OPs until no unsatisfied OPs or necessary NEs remain.
+> Trace every element OP through receivers back to the external CQU.
+> After trace closure, resurvey all functionality and record any unreached functionality under the CQU whose OP it serves; functionality already contained by a parent remains expressed through that parent.
+> Seek SEs for every AUE.
+> Detect obvious drift/errors during tracing: intended functionality absent=>MISS; incorrect/nonworking code=>BKN; apparent non-belonging=>exclude; attach concern to its unique element type with references; do not solve.
+> Anneal shared PE subfunctions into load-bearing parent functions where parent purpose can carry them; otherwise retain independently.
+> Preserve absorbed subpart purpose exclusively as subtype joins refining the matching parent purpose join; never optimize atomic functionality away.
+> Final recorded map is minimal, coarse, shallow, annealed, yet complete in parent functionality.
+> Proof/read back the entire map against artifact + specification; correct, anneal, complete.
+> Final graph has exactly one root AUE with every mapped element/join beneath it and nothing disconnected.
+> Namespace entries are discrete functional roles instantiated by the artifact at the most specific reusable type level.
+> Use specific mechanisms, never vague top-level labels when a specific functional type exists.
+> Namespace identity remains type-level; joins carry AUE-specific OP/EF.
+> A join speaks about this AUE's actual particulars; representations express their function within the AUE, not the represented object's independent real-world function.
+> One or more distinct CQUs must hold objective purposes served by the DE through distinct encounter functions where applicable.
+> Intake is never gated or judged; only its resulting map may later be graded/refined.
+> Infer CQUs from the artifact type, not from whoever requested/performs the intake.
+> CQU means the reusable party/role whose purpose drives artifact changes/improvement; when one person holds multiple roles, use the role that changes the artifact.
+> Prefer the CQU driving the most improvement.
+> CQU is never generic "operator", "end user", "developer", or requester merely because they operate/use/build the artifact; developer is valid only where development itself is the artifact's functional domain (e.g. IDE/programming tool).
+> CQU examples preserve source semantics: media.photo seller/social-media-poster/blogger valid; buyer/insurance-company/operator invalid; document.story Reader valid.
+> Namespace is typological ontology, not taxonomy; no filler domain/class segments or fixed depth.
+> Namespace address MUST reverse by periods→spaces into its valid noun name; child reversed names inherit parent as final noun.
+> Namespace narrows trunk→leaf; each entry is its parent type or a function within it, never non-functionality.
+> Namespace entries name functional approaches as proper nouns.
+> Multiword functional variants use separate segments when prefixes independently form valid types; underscore only when no constituent forms a valid prefix and reversed name remains correct.
+> Set name_length to the accepted short-name lookback segment count.
+> Use established practitioner terminology; forbid coined, bespoke, abstract-pattern, shorthand, colloquial, marketing, encoding/language/style labels. If no standard term exists, use plain common functional noun.
+> During refinement/correction, audit all existing namespace paths and execute corrections for violations.
+> `name` is exact project canonical name when specified; otherwise industry term; CQU name is inferred industry role title.
+> Validity anchors: code.engine.game valid; code.game/code.game.engine invalid; code.engine.game.fps valid by distinct functionality; code.engine.game.platformer invalid; media.image/media.asset.image/media.photo/media.photo.scenery valid; media.photo.jpg/code.cpp/document.word.story.conflict invalid; document.story.conflict valid.
+> Generate result id at intake start and expose it as metaform id; it exists for later deep-result linkage.
+> Record through intake tools; schema defines object fields and is not returned as a document.
+> Element identity is namespace_address only; all references use namespace_address, never readable name alone.
+> All namespace records are elements.
+> Single root element = AUE addressed by AT with role=AUE.
+> CQUs are role=CQU directly beneath root, never DE|SE|NE.
+> Internal AUE elements have exactly one role DE|SE|NE.
+> PE is never a role; PE is the element nested in a join.
+> Same element may be RE/CQU in one relationship and PE in another without duplication.
+> First/full PE occurrence contains its elements/joins; repeated PE references contain namespace_address,name_length,name,role only.
+> Every join connects RE(OP)→nested PE(EF) and carries type,purpose,ef,ifd.
+> purpose joins may contain subtype joins for annealed subparts.
!> Do not deepen intake through non-functional variants.
!> Do not name Parametrics.
!> Do not solve encountered problems during intake.
!> Do not duplicate namespace records for an element already mapped.
!> Do not leave absorbed subparts as independent elements.
!> Do not leave free-floating/disconnected elements.
!> Do not coin terminology or encode medium/encoding/language/style/genre as functionality.
!> Do not substitute generic operator/user/developer/requester for the inferred CQU.
!> Do not return the schema as a result document.

@CONDITION:
?IF (collection/folder) -> {State}:=SURVEY_ALL
?IF (unmapped AUE remains) -> {State}:=CLASSIFY
?IF (AT needs external receiver) -> {State}:=CQU
?IF (unsatisfied OP OR required NE remains) -> {State}:=TRACE
?IF (drift/error observed) -> {State}:=FLAG
?IF (trace exhausted) -> {State}:=CLOSURE
?IF (closure complete) -> {State}:=ANNEAL
?IF (annealed) -> {State}:=PROOF
?IF (proof valid AND one connected root) -> {Complete}:=TRUE
:ELSE -> {State}:=CORRECT

@ROUTER:
@MATCH({State}):
| [SURVEY]     -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Survey)
| [SURVEY_ALL] -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Survey)
| [CLASSIFY]   -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Classify)
| [CQU]        -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(CQU)
| [TRACE]      -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Trace)
| [FLAG]       -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Flag)
| [CLOSURE]    -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Closure)
| [ANNEAL]     -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Anneal)
| [PROOF]      -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Proof)
| [CORRECT]    -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Correct)

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Survey):
∇({Target},{Prompt}) => read intent/artifacts deeply; inventory every AUE; model expected functionality; observe DE/SE/NE and OP/EF distinctions
=> {State}:=CLASSIFY

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Classify):
∇(each AUE) => determine functional AT independent of medium/encoding/genre/style; group only equivalent functional imperatives
Δ(AUE,AT) => create/identify singular AT-root candidate; {State}:=CQU

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(CQU):
∇(AT,DE) => infer specific reusable beneficiary-role whose OP drives greatest improvement
Δ(CQU,OP,DE.EF) => record CQU + purpose join; CHECK BKN/MISS; {State}:=TRACE

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Trace):
∇(current RE.OP) => find PE whose EF serves it; determine ifd; identify DE/SE/NE; inspect PE requirements/OPs
Δ(RE,PE) => record element/join immediately; enqueue PE OPs; CHECK BKN/MISS
=> continue TRACE until {Open_OP} empty

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Flag):
∇(observation) => classify absent-intended=MISS | incorrect/nonworking=BKN | apparent-nonmember=exclude
Δ(flag) => attach to unique functional element with references; return TRACE

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Closure):
∇(survey,map) => find functionality not reached
Δ(each missing function) => find its CQU OP and record join OR retain inside already-named parent functionality
=> {State}:=ANNEAL

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Anneal):
∇(PE subfunctions,shared integration joins) => find parent macro-functions
?IF (parent purpose carries subpart purpose)
 -> Δ(subpart) => remove independent element; preserve as subtype join inside parent's matching purpose join
:ELSE
 -> retain independent functional element
=> repeat until final coarse functional shape; {State}:=PROOF

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Proof):
∇(whole map,artifact,specification) => verify function coverage, namespace legality, roles, references, joins, annealing, canonical names, connectedness
?IF (all valid) -> {Complete}:=TRUE
:ELSE -> {State}:=CORRECT

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Correct):
Δ(proof defects) => correct map without inventing functionality; rerun ANNEAL then PROOF

@VERIFY:
{Valid}:=
({Complete}=TRUE)
AND (exactly one AUE root exists)
AND (all records descend from root)
AND (all namespace references resolve by namespace_address)
AND (roles obey AUE|CQU|DE|SE|NE semantics AND PE is not a role)
AND (each mapped join has type,purpose,ef,ifd,nested PE)
AND (all relevant CQU OP→PE EF relationships are represented)
AND (SE search performed for every AUE)
AND (no required parent functionality omitted)
AND (Parametrics absent)
AND (genre/style/medium/encoding/language/non-functionality absent from type structure)
AND (namespace reversibility,trunk→leaf,functionality,terminology,name_length,name rules pass)
AND (drift flags preserve evidence without solving)
AND (absorbed subparts exist only as subtype refinements)
AND (map is final annealed coarse/shallow shape)
AND (no disconnected/free-floating element exists)

{Schema}:=
<metaform id="[result id]" name="[project]" description="[AT/AUE description]">
 <elements><element namespace_address="AT" name_length="#" name="canonical" role="AUE">
  <elements><element namespace_address="stakeholder.*" name_length="#" name="industry role" role="CQU">
   <joins><join type="purpose" purpose="OP" ef="PE EF" ifd="send|receive|both">
    <elements><element namespace_address="*" name_length="#" name="canonical" role="DE|SE|NE"><elements/><joins/></element></elements>
    <joins><join type="subtype" purpose="parent-purpose refinement" ef="subpart EF" ifd="send|receive|both"/></joins>
   </join></joins>
  </element></elements>
 </element></elements>
</metaform>
